    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose 76.18 efficiency score makes him our primary offensive engine. Facing a favorable matchup against Bennett, **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a substantial park boost and a slow delivery from the opposing starter that elevates his stolen base potential, a critical factor for our internal weighting. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** follows closely at 67.93, as his favorable matchup against Bibee allows him to drive the middle of our order, while **Coby Mayo** (66.72) and **Kyle Tucker** (65.50) provide the requisite power-speed upside to keep our categorical production high. **Henry Bolte** also projects as a strong start at 65.00, assuming he occupies the leadoff spot; his combination of SP skill and optimal lineup placement makes him a high-leverage asset against Kade Anderson.\n\nStrategic benching remains vital to managing our remaining game caps, and today\u2019s most difficult decision involved **Miguel Vargas**. While **Miguel Vargas** posted a respectable 52.56 score with an impressive .389 xwOBA, the volatility of his platoon advantage and his lower overall efficiency relative to our starters kept him on the pine. We are monitoring lineup confirmations for **Tommy White** and **Kyle Tucker**, as their current scores rely on assumed batting orders; should **Tommy White** be pushed down the lineup or face an unexpected defensive substitution, we risk losing the efficiency gains baked into his 58.64 projection. While we are relieved to see no major weather alerts, the heavy reliance on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** against the tricky Bennett requires us to keep a close eye on early-inning plate discipline to ensure these high-score projections hold against a respectable 3.99 xERA.",
